# Licence texts are redistributed BYTE-VERBATIM, so nothing in this directory
# may be line-ending converted.
#
# This is not a style preference. core.autocrlf is true on the Windows seat, and
# with the default text=auto a fresh clone would write these files back out with
# CRLF -- a different file, byte for byte, from the one that was fetched and
# hashed. The SHA-256 values recorded in PROVENANCE.md would then match nothing
# on disk, and the provenance record would quietly become false on every Windows
# checkout while remaining true on Linux.
#
# -text disables the conversion in both directions, so the blob, the worktree
# and the staged installer all carry the same bytes on every platform.
* -text
